That's right; it's a 1/13 chance. So it's good policy to put
away any gold, but have some unidentified items in your main
inventory, before #sit'ting on the throne. thrn-343.txt says
"Items in inventory are NOT at risk of explosion." so you can
have unIDed wands and rings.

Also: Quaffing at a non-magic fountain can give enlightenment
(1/30 chance). (As David Damerell mentions in the ID spoiler,
enlightenment can help you ID worn amulets and rings.) Of
course, you also get a 1/30 chance of cursing things in your
inventory, so this doesn't seem worthwhile.

Sadly, in this my first illiterate game, I didn't find any
!oEnli or /oEnli and no throne gave an ID.

A few other misc. notes that weren't in the ID spoiler; first
two can be risky if you're not prepared for the consequences:

 - You can identify =3DoFA by hitting a gelcube or similar ("You
   stiffen momentarily.").

 - You can identify =3DoSD by the fact that purple worms, lurkers
   above, etc. will spit you out ("doesn't like your taste"). I
   have seen that message a lot, and it never dawned on me why
   (duh). TDTTOE

 - You can identify /oSDD by the fact that it's the only NODIR
   wand that produces no obvious effect. Kieron Dunbar's wand ID
   spoiler mentions this.

   1. Use the techniques described in the ID spoiler to identify
      other no-engrave wands like open, lock, etc. by zapping
      them at specific things.

   2. When zapping the no-engrave wands, watch for one that
      doesn't ask for a direction, and does nothing (meaning:
      does not produce any message or visible effect). That's
      /oSDD.

   3. Of course, this depends on the wand's charges; once you
      see "Nothing happens." that wand is empty, and you can't
      test it further.


